---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  MonsterAvatarBuilder,
  MonsterAvatarGallery,
  MonsterAvatarMotions,
  MonsterAvatarSizes,
} from '../../components/MonsterAvatarDemo';
---

<Docs title="Monster Avatar" description="Animated monster characters for agents, mixed from swappable parts.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Monster Avatar</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A friendly monster for each agent. Pick a body, color, pattern, ears, eyes, mouth, hat, and the thing it holds, or
    let the agent id choose. Each one breathes, blinks, and moves the thing it holds.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <MonsterAvatarSizes client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Monster avatar"
      code={`import { MonsterAvatar, monsterAvatarPresets } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/monster-avatar";

<MonsterAvatar agentId={agent.id} size={48} />
<MonsterAvatar color="yellow" hat="headphones" item="email" />
<MonsterAvatar config={monsterAvatarPresets[0].config} label="Marketing agent" />`}
    />
    <p>
      Part props override the character from <code>agentId</code> or <code>config</code>. Pass
      <code>animated={'{false}'}</code> for a still avatar. Use <code>monsterAvatarSrc(config)</code> for a still
      <code>data:</code> URL.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Mix your own</h2>
    <MonsterAvatarBuilder client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Animations</h2>
    <p>
      Every monster breathes and blinks. What it holds sets the rest of its motion, and each avatar starts at its own
      point in the loop so a grid never moves in step.
    </p>
    <MonsterAvatarMotions client:visible />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Presets</h2>
    <MonsterAvatarGallery client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Performance</h2>
    <p>
      The artwork is inline SVG, built from strings and cached, with no images to load. Breathing, blinking, and item
      motion are CSS animations that change only <code>transform</code> and <code>opacity</code> on separate layers, so
      the browser runs them on the compositor. A shared observer pauses avatars that are off screen, and they stay still
      when the user prefers reduced motion.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Without <code>label</code> the avatar is decorative and hidden from assistive technology. Put the agent's name in
      nearby text, or pass <code>label</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
